hex files for the bootloader stub code now come in two flavours,
'charger compulsory' and 'charger not compulsory'
functionally, they are identical, and indeed built from the same code base,
with the exception that 'charger compulsory' versions require the charger to be plugged in
to permit an update ,whereas "charger not compulsory' will attempt an update 
without charger plugged in
These two variants have their own sub directory, appropriately named


Thus hex files will have a suffix 'CC' or 'CNC' following the version number.

